\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Depth of mercy! can there be
\par Mercy still reserved for me?
\par Can my God His wrath forbear?
\par Me, the Chief of sinners, spare?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I have long withstood His grace,
\par Long provoked Him to His face,
\par Would not hearken to His calls,
\par Grieved Him by a thousand falls.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 3. Whence to me this waste of love?
\par Ask my Advocate above!
\par See the cause in Jesu's face,
\par Now before the throne of grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There for me the Saviour stands;
\par Shows His wounds and spreads His hands.
\par God is love; I know, I feel;
\par Jesus lives, and loves me still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Jesus, answer from above:
\par Is not all Thy nature love?
\par Wilt Thou not the wrong forget?
\par Suffer me to kiss Thy feet?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Pity from Thine eye let fall;
\par By a look my soul recall;
\par Now the stone to flesh convert,
\par Cast a look, and break my heart.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

